  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The plot given below shows <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> curves (where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> is the pressure and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> is the temperature) for two solvents <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> and isomolal solutions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> in these solvents. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> is completely dissociates in both the solvents.<br ><img src=\"assets\\qt0008_12ab625aa2a0.png\"/><br >On the addition of equal number of moles of a non-volatile solute <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> in equal amount (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kg</mi></math>) of these solvents, the elevation of boiling point of solvent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> is three times that of solvent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>. The solute <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> is known to undergo dimerization in these solvents. If the degree of dimerization is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn></math> in the solvent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>, the degree of dimerization in the solvent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> is _______.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "0.05",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From the graph:<br >For the solvent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>,    </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><msub><mtext>T</mtext><mi>bx</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><msub><mtext>T</mtext><mi>bx</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi>NaCl</mi></msub><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math><br >For the solvent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>,   </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><msub><mtext>T</mtext><mi>by</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><msub><mtext>T</mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi>NaCl</mi></msub><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math><br >From the equations (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></math>) and (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ii</mi></math>),<br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br >For the solute <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>,<br ><img src=\"assets\\st0008_98e788192fc4.jpg\"/><br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mtext>α</mtext><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><msub><mtext>T</mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext>α</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub></math><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><msub><mtext>T</mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext>α</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub></math><br >Given: </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><msub><mtext>T</mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>∆</mo><msub><mtext>T</mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub></math><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext>α</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext>α</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub></math><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext>α</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext>α</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>α</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.7</mo></math><br >So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>α</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.05</mo></math></p>"
  }
